bench_local30_gen.py is a benchmark script that generates answers for the       
"hard-30" query set using the local Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B model (served via       
Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Its key features are:                     

 • Local Generation: Runs entirely on a local machine (e.g., a 64GB Mac) using  
   Ollama, avoiding cloud costs.                                                
 • Incremental Persistence: Saves generated answers to                          
   eval_candidates_local30_hard.json incrementally, allowing recovery from      
   crashes.                                                                     
 • Resume Support: Skips queries that already have answers in the output file.  
 • Error Handling: Logs errors for failed requests and continues processing.    
 • Demo Mode: Includes an offline self-check (--demo) that verifies logic       
   without calling Ollama.                                                      

The script outputs a JSON file mapping query IDs to a list of candidate answers 
(with model name, content, latency, and error info), which is then used by      
bench_local30_grade.py for head-to-head comparison against the 80B model.       

